二、English Terms
────────────────────────────────────────

1. Definitions
   "Software" means the original or adapted source code, docs, and assets in this repository that are owned by the copyright holder (excluding third-party components and their original licenses).
   "Open Source License" means any OSI-approved or commonly called open-source license (including without limitation MIT, Apache, BSD, GPL, LGPL, MPL, AGPL), or any license that requires or permits public re-licensing/redistribution as open source.
   "Re-Open-Sourcing" means publishing, redistributing, or re-licensing the Software (or a modification/derivative) under an Open Source License, or offering it to the public as an "open source" project.

2. Grant (Use Allowed)
   Subject to this License, the copyright holder grants you a worldwide, royalty-free, non-transferable, non-exclusive license to:
   (a) run, study, and research the Software;
   (b) copy and modify the Software for personal use or internal use within your organization;
   (c) distribute copies inside your organization solely for such internal use (not as a public open-source release).

3. Restrictions (No Re-Open-Sourcing)
   Without prior written permission from the copyright holder, you may not:
   (a) publish, redistribute, or re-license the Software (or any modification/derivative) under any Open Source License;
   (b) represent the Software as "Open Source" when redistributing or re-licensing it to the public;
   (c) remove or alter copyright notices, this License, or third-party notices required by NOTICE;
   (d) use the copyright holder's trademarks, logos, or project name to imply endorsement, partnership, or official affiliation (except fair attribution required by law).

4. Third-Party Components
   vn.py, vnpy_ctp, and other dependencies remain under their own licenses (often MIT). This License covers only this repository's original/wrapper code and does not supersede third-party licenses. You must comply with those licenses separately.

5. Reservation of Rights
   All rights not expressly granted are reserved. Ownership of the Software does not transfer under this License.

6. Disclaimer
   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NONINFRINGEMENT. TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, THE COPYRIGHT HOLDER SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY DAMAGES ARISING FROM USE OF THE SOFTWARE.

7. Termination
   This License terminates automatically if you breach it. Upon termination you must stop using and destroy copies obtained under this License (except as required by law).

